<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 44 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as James, son of Zebedee, Saint James the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James the Great, son of Zebedee, was one of the twelve apostles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>, executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-agrippa-i">Herod Agrippa I</a> around 44 CE. Medieval tradition held that his body had been carried to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, and the discovery of his supposed tomb at Compostela in the early 9th century, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ii-of-asturias">Alfonso II of Asturias</a>, created one of Christendom's great pilgrimage centres and made him patron of Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-the-great.jpg" alt="James the Great" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Paul Rubens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_St_James_the_Apostle_-_WGA20192.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…on the Apocalypse around 776 and attacked the Adoptionist teaching of Archbishop Elipandus of Toledo, and the discovery of what was believed to be the tomb of <b>Saint James</b> the Apostle at Compostela in the early ninth century began a cult that drew pilgrims from across Latin Europe.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-asturias">Kingdom of Asturias · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Galicia had been the core of the Kingdom of the Suebi and a part of the Asturian realm, and the cult of <b>St James</b> at Compostela had made it famous across Europe.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-galicia">Kingdom of Galicia</a></li></ul></section>
